source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-23
observed: Jira opens an empty square item to hold the round one the run's last character asks for; JFM keeps the line visible rather than fabricating that parent.
-- input.jira --
-* item
-- rendered.html --
<ul class="alternate" type="square">
	<li>
	<ul>
		<li>item</li>
	</ul>
	</li>
</ul>
-- want.md --
\-\* item
-- warnings.json --
[
  {
    "Line": 1,
    "Column": 1,
    "Construct": "list",
    "Reason": "list item has no parent at its authored nesting level"
  }
]
